   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. Several stereo assignments are assumed rather than read from the wedges.\n\n**Structure as I read it**\n- **Sugar arms:** three identical GalNAc units, each a \u03b2-O-glycoside with an N-acetyl group, linked through O-(CH2)4-C(=O)-NH-(CH2)3-NH-C(=O)-CH2CH2-O-CH2-. All three arms attach to one central quaternary carbon.\n- **Spacer:** the central carbon carries an NH-C(=O)-CH2CH2- group, then nine O units separated by CH2CH2, then CH2CH2-C(=O)-NH. This amide is attached to the Lys side-chain \u03b5-nitrogen of the peptide.\n- **Cyclic peptide:** the ring runs Lys, Asn, Tyr, Sar (N-methylglycine), Arg, Asp, Tic (tetrahydroisoquinoline-3-carboxylic acid), Asn, N-Me-Phe, then Cys, which carries a C-terminal Gly-NH2. The ring closes through a thioether: a chloroacetyl-derived CH2-S bridge links the Cys sulfur to the N-terminal Phe. From that Phe the chain continues Arg, N-Me-Phe, Ser, and back to the Lys nitrogen.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- The sugar stereocentres are written as \u03b2-D-GalNAc, applied identically to all three arms.\n- The amino acids are written as L, including Tic, because I could not reliably resolve each wedge in the image.\n\nI wrote the peptide ring in the C\u2192N direction so that the ring-closure digits and chirality tags stay consistent.\n\nSMILES: C(COCCC(=O)NCCCNC(=O)CCCCO[C@@H]1O[C@H](CO)[C@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]1NC(C)=O)(COCCC(=O)NCCCNC(=O)CCCCO[C@@H]1O[C@H](CO)[C@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]1NC(C)=O)(COCCC(=O)NCCCNC(=O)CCCCO[C@@H]1O[C@H](CO)[C@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]1NC(C)=O)NC(=O)CCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCC(=O)NCCCC[C@@H]2NC(=O)[C@H](CO)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccccc1)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(N)=N)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccccc1)NC(=O)CSC[C@@H](C(=O)NCC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccccc1)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@@H]3Cc4ccccc4CN3C(=O)[C@H](CC(=O)O)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(N)=N)NC(=O)CN(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc(O)cc1)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC2=O"
